spelled my way is one of 'em.

00:22:34.610 --> 00:22:36.310
So I'm like okay it's good enough.

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:40.640
But it's really more about the event of,

00:22:40.640 --> 00:22:43.150
getting this group of people
together that we've never been

00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:45.370
on vacation together,
like I have not vacationed

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:47.920
with my brother and my parents

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.410
since we did vacations as kids.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:51.970
Mm-hmm.

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:55.963
And Micah, my oldest nephew,

00:22:57.760 --> 00:23:00.100
is going into his senior
year in high school

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:02.240
so I was like this might be the last time

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:05.260
that we're all available to
just go on a trip together

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:08.069
and I had this idea like
it'll be fun to go over there,

00:23:08.069 --> 00:23:13.069
we'll go meet the chief, we'll get kilts,

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:14.913
we'll take pictures.

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:17.070
Family photo.

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:19.920
And that'll make it all worth it.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.550
Now, so we were in the process
of working out the details

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:25.850
in order to make what I
just described happen.

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.820
And one of the things I
was concerned about is

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:32.520
my mom has become less
mobile over the past,

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:36.920
she's getting older and so
she's become less mobile

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:40.810
and I knew that going over
to, she can still walk

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:43.150
and everything but she's
just walking more slowly

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:46.330
and steps and long distances
and that kinda thing

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:47.733
become sort of a concern.

00:23:48.590 --> 00:23:53.590
So I knew that going to a country as old,

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:58.120
a civilization as old as
Scotland was, you know,

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:03.120
it's not like there's a bunch
of ramps and stuff around.

00:24:03.610 --> 00:24:06.060
We're talking about castles,
we're talking about stone steps

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:08.590
that are not up to modern day codes.

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:10.600
So I knew there'd be a lot of walking

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:12.940
and so what I did and I
think I've talked about this

00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:15.550
but I got her a trainer
back in North Carolina,

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:16.660
somebody who can meet with her

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:20.560
and basically help her
work out and get stronger

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:23.190
and get her legs stronger
and that kinda thing

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:26.970
so she'd been doing that
for seven or eight months

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:29.210
leading up to the trip.

00:24:29.210 --> 00:24:32.240
So she was open to that,
she was cool with that.

00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:33.747
Yeah.
That's good.

00:24:33.747 --> 00:24:35.380
I mean it took a little
bit of talking her into it

00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:38.390
but then she did it and
she loved it and she would,

00:24:38.390 --> 00:24:40.550
I talked her to her on the
phone and she would say

00:24:40.550 --> 00:24:42.130
I'm having a great time with my trainer.

00:24:42.130 --> 00:24:44.450
Even the trainer kinda
switched in the middle

00:24:44.450 --> 00:24:47.807
'cause one woman left and
she got a guy that came in

00:24:47.807 --> 00:24:49.817
but she's like, "I love my trainer.

00:24:49.817 --> 00:24:51.507
"I love what I'm doing,
I'm getting stronger,

00:24:51.507 --> 00:24:52.440
"I'm feeling good."

00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.860
Sometimes when a trainer
switches, you don't even notice.

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.610
You've seen that magic
trick where it's like--

00:24:56.610 --> 00:24:57.443
The trainer switch.

00:24:57.443 --> 00:24:58.950
A guy can kind of come in--
David Blaine,

00:24:58.950 --> 00:25:00.100
David Blaine invented that.

00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:02.890
And become a different
person you won't even notice.

00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:03.903
Criss Angel maybe.

00:25:06.722 --> 00:25:08.229
I think it was that red-headed--

00:25:08.229 --> 00:25:10.620
Carrot Top.
Mormon magician on YouTube.

00:25:10.620 --> 00:25:12.080
I don't know about him.

00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:13.552
He's the guy--
But I'm interested--

00:25:14.605 --> 00:25:16.170
He does the switch, man.

00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:21.170
So you know, we get
there and I said earlier

00:25:22.630 --> 00:25:25.460
that the forecast was
rain basically every day

00:25:25.460 --> 00:25:27.410
and we experienced a lot
of rain the first day

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:31.106
but then it kinda cleared up
and it would rain a little bit

00:25:31.106 --> 00:25:34.730
but we had all the sunlight
that we needed to do

00:25:34.730 --> 00:25:36.180
the things that we had
planned for each day.

00:25:36.180 --> 00:25:39.360
I kinda had a thing that
we were gonna do every day.

00:25:39.360 --> 00:25:42.820
We saw Edinburgh, we saw the castle,

00:25:42.820 --> 00:25:47.410
we took a tour of Mary King's
Close which is basically

00:25:47.410 --> 00:25:49.903
how they built the city up over centuries

00:25:49.903 --> 00:25:53.210
and you can go down and my
mom took all these steps

00:25:53.210 --> 00:25:54.327
and she kept comin' up and she's like,

00:25:54.327 --> 00:25:55.557
"I couldn't have done this without

00:25:55.557 --> 00:25:57.250
"that training I've been doing."

00:25:57.250 --> 00:26:00.117
She kept coming up to
me and just saying like,

00:26:00.117 --> 00:26:02.247
"This has been so helpful.

00:26:02.247 --> 00:26:03.837
"I wouldn't be doing this."

00:26:05.702 --> 00:26:10.702
And then we go to Glencoe
and we do a day of falconry.

00:26:10.890 --> 00:26:11.730
Falconry?

00:26:11.730 --> 00:26:16.730
I got a guide to, had this hawk named Elsa

00:26:17.800 --> 00:26:20.190
that we all got to spend time with

00:26:20.190 --> 00:26:23.730
and she would fly off and
then we'd put some chicken

00:26:23.730 --> 00:26:25.970
on our hand and she
would come and fly back

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:28.230
and eat it and everybody did it.

00:26:28.230 --> 00:26:31.050
When I was at Ko Samui, I
went to a falcon sanctuary

00:26:31.050 --> 00:26:33.150
where they don't make 'em do that anymore.

00:26:35.490 --> 00:26:37.870
Just kidding.

00:26:37.870 --> 00:26:40.710
She seemed to be happy.

00:26:40.710 --> 00:26:44.450
So, and also on that day,
we were supposed to get rain

00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:45.580
and it didn't rain.

00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:48.330
I was just like this
is just going so well.

00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:50.510
Everything is going well.
Oh yeah.

00:26:50.510 --> 00:26:52.990
The weather's great,
and then, the next day--

00:26:52.990 --> 00:26:56.130
To your credit.
Yeah yeah, the next day,

00:26:56.130 --> 00:27:00.560
we're gonna go and the plan
is we're gonna go down to,

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:02.870
we're gonna drive like an hour or so south

00:27:02.870 --> 00:27:06.331
of Glencoe, we're gonna go
to the old Lachlan castle.

00:27:06.331 --> 00:27:09.240
We're gonna meet the chief of the clan.

00:27:09.240 --> 00:27:10.240
Yes.

00:27:10.240 --> 00:27:12.400
We're gonna hang out with
him for a little bit.

00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:13.260
Yeah.

00:27:13.260 --> 00:27:16.480
And then we're gonna go to--
Maybe knock back a few.

00:27:16.480 --> 00:27:20.620
We're gonna meet a photographer
Paul, that's his name.

00:27:20.620 --> 00:27:24.100
And he's going to, oh, we're
going to get into full garb:

00:27:24.100 --> 00:27:25.300
kilts--

00:27:25.300 --> 00:27:26.650
Bagpipes.
Kilts basically.

00:27:26.650 --> 00:27:30.340
No bagpipes involved and we were gonna try

00:27:30.340 --> 00:27:32.820
to do the MacLachlan tartan
'cause every family has

00:27:32.820 --> 00:27:35.060
their own tartan but
they didn't have enough.

00:27:35.060 --> 00:27:39.370
We used just a general
Scotland millennium tartan.

00:27:39.370 --> 00:27:40.730
Still looked very Scottish.

00:27:40.730 --> 00:27:43.266
Now is a tartan just a
pattern or is it a flag?

00:27:43.266 --> 00:27:45.520
It's a pattern, it's
basically what we would,

00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:47.700
just dumb rednecks would call plaid.

00:27:47.700 --> 00:27:49.020
It's a type--
Special plaid.

00:27:49.020 --> 00:27:51.311
It's a type of plaid, man.
Okay.

00:27:51.311 --> 00:27:53.440
And every family has their own

00:27:53.440 --> 00:27:55.133
and you go into these shops,
they're all around Scotland,

00:27:55.133 --> 00:27:58.840
it's like here's all the
families, all the clans,

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:00.160
and here's their special tartan

00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:02.750
and it's like the MacLachlan
tartan has an old tartan

00:28:02.750 --> 00:28:04.771
and a new tartan.
Wow.

00:28:04.771 --> 00:28:06.910
And there's tartans for special events

00:28:06.910 --> 00:28:09.310
and all kinds of things, anyway.

00:28:09.310 --> 00:28:14.310
So we've got dressed and
got completely in the stuff

00:28:15.350 --> 00:28:18.010
at the hotel basically so
we were all ready to go.

00:28:18.010 --> 00:28:19.520
Everybody's looking great, feeling great,

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:20.690
we did put--
Kinda feels like

00:28:20.690 --> 00:28:21.990
a wedding day.
It's a lot like

00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:23.790
a wedding day 'cause
this is how traditional,

00:28:23.790 --> 00:28:26.150
this is how Scottish
people dress for weddings.

00:28:26.150 --> 00:28:28.120
That's what the kilts
are for most of the time,

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:29.935
formal events and weddings.

00:28:29.935 --> 00:28:31.500
And for Braveheart.
We put the kilts

00:28:31.500 --> 00:28:32.550
on backwards.

00:28:32.550 --> 00:28:34.970
I will say that, until then
we looked at the picture

00:28:34.970 --> 00:28:37.310
on the internet and just,
it's real easy to fix that,

00:28:37.310 --> 00:28:39.460
you just turn it.
Turn it around.

00:28:39.460 --> 00:28:40.393
180 degrees.

00:28:41.330 --> 00:28:43.190
So again it's supposed--
Because it's a skirt

00:28:43.190 --> 00:28:44.634
for men.
Yeah it's supposed

00:28:44.634 --> 00:28:47.900
to start raining, not only--

00:28:47.900 --> 00:28:48.733
It's like a purse for men.

00:28:48.733 --> 00:28:50.873
Speaking of fanny packs.
Yeah?

00:28:52.340 --> 00:28:55.270
I put the thing on, I'm like,
there's no pockets in this.

00:28:55.270 --> 00:28:56.950
Well there's this thing.

00:28:56.950 --> 00:28:58.700
Jenna you can look up the
official name of this.

00:28:58.700 --> 00:28:59.890
I can't remember it now.

00:28:59.890 --> 00:29:03.180
There's a purse that you
wear right over your crotch

00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:04.597
and that's where you keep all your stuff.

00:29:04.597 --> 00:29:05.543
So--

00:29:05.543 --> 00:29:07.860
A Scottish crotch patch.
So Scottish men

00:29:07.860 --> 00:29:11.750
are the ones who came up with
skirts and purses for men.

00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:14.120
Own it man, come on!
The most manly men

00:29:14.120 --> 00:29:17.080
in the world are okay with
wearing skirts and purses.

00:29:17.080 --> 00:29:19.713
The water's fine, jump right in.

00:29:22.030 --> 00:29:24.302
So, she'll find out what it's called.

00:29:24.302 --> 00:29:26.220
I think the most manly men
in the world are wrestlers

00:29:26.220 --> 00:29:27.053
but whatever.

00:29:27.053 --> 00:29:29.000
Well there's Scottish wrestlers.

00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:30.041
The Bushwhackers.

00:29:30.041 --> 00:29:31.900
They were New Zealanders right?

00:29:31.900 --> 00:29:33.100
You talking about Rowdy Roddy Piper?

00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:35.160
Yeah exactly, no he's Irish.

00:29:35.160 --> 00:29:36.630
I don't know maybe he's Scottish.

00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:40.150
He was a bagpiper.
So yeah, Scottish yeah.

00:29:40.150 --> 00:29:42.743
So it's called a sporran, yeah, a sporran.

00:29:44.769 --> 00:29:47.170
And so--
S-P-O-R-R-A-N?

00:29:47.170 --> 00:29:48.010
Yes.

00:29:48.010 --> 00:29:52.100
And so we've got our sporrans
and our knee-high socks.

00:29:52.100 --> 00:29:53.775
Freakin' fanny packs.

00:29:53.775 --> 00:29:55.479
Look like a bunch of
school girls, it's great.

00:29:55.479 --> 00:29:56.312
Dang.

00:29:56.312 --> 00:30:00.150
And it's supposed to
rain at like 11:30 based

00:30:00.150 --> 00:30:02.060
on the forecast and
11:30's when we're supposed

00:30:02.060 --> 00:30:03.310
to meet the photographer.

00:30:04.980 --> 00:30:09.070
But okay, so we pull
up to the new castles.

00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:11.483
There's the old castle ruin
and then there's the new castle

00:30:11.483 --> 00:30:14.310
and the new castle, you can stay there.

00:30:14.310 --> 00:30:16.200
It's got a restaurant, hotel, whatever

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:19.480
and it's also where Ewan MacLachlan lives,

00:30:19.480 --> 00:30:20.440
the chief.

00:30:20.440 --> 00:30:22.923
Does it look like an old castle?

00:30:22.923 --> 00:30:24.600
The old or the new castle?

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:26.970
The new one.
New castle just looks like,

00:30:26.970 --> 00:30:30.850
I mean it was built in the
1700s so it's still pretty old.

00:30:30.850 --> 00:30:35.030
It looks like a house but
like a old-school house

00:30:35.030 --> 00:30:38.330
that you might call a castle
but not like stone spires

00:30:38.330 --> 00:30:39.840
and stuff like that, it's like white.

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:42.450
The one in your Instagram that I saw.

00:30:42.450 --> 00:30:44.160
That's the old castle.
That's the old castle.

00:30:44.160 --> 00:30:45.030
Which is still standing,

00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:47.220
it's a ruin but it's still standing.

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:48.053
Okay.

00:30:50.690 --> 00:30:53.530
So we pull up, we meet the chief

00:30:53.530 --> 00:30:55.550
and then we meet basically the chairman

00:30:55.550 --> 00:31:00.200
of the MacLachlan clan worldwide
who kinda took us around.

00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:03.700
He ended up taking us, he's
the one that kinda took us

00:31:03.700 --> 00:31:08.050
around to most of the stuff
and kinda like gave us a tour

00:31:08.050 --> 00:31:09.980
of things and would give
us information about stuff.

00:31:09.980 --> 00:31:10.940
What was he like?

00:31:10.940 --> 00:31:13.570
Was he yelling in a Scottish accent?

00:31:13.570 --> 00:31:15.860
No he actually had a British accent.

00:31:15.860 --> 00:31:20.860
Because he grew up in England but he is a,

00:31:20.920 --> 00:31:22.010
he's a MacLachlan so--

00:31:22.010 --> 00:31:24.570
But was he yelling like it was like

00:31:24.570 --> 00:31:26.220
about to go into a battle?

00:31:26.220 --> 00:31:28.179
No, that's in the movies, Link.

00:31:28.179 --> 00:31:32.410
He's just pretty much a
mild-mannered, well-tempered man.

00:31:32.410 --> 00:31:33.620
Was he in a kilt?

00:31:33.620 --> 00:31:36.470
Yes, he was definitely in
a kilt and they were both

00:31:36.470 --> 00:31:37.630
in the MacLachlan tartan.

00:31:37.630 --> 00:31:40.400
He was in the old school
MacLachlan tartan the whole time.

00:31:40.400 --> 00:31:44.690
Was the chief, had a
gruff beard, a gruff voice

00:31:44.690 --> 00:31:47.410
and was he gnawing on a chicken leg?

00:31:47.410 --> 00:31:51.610
I'll show you a picture
of my dad with the chief.

00:31:51.610 --> 00:31:53.073
And what was his demeanor?

00:31:54.020 --> 00:31:56.160
His demeanor is as captured

00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:58.283
and there he is with the chief.

00:31:59.240 --> 00:32:01.280
Which one's which, dude?

00:32:01.280 --> 00:32:02.460
They're freakin'--

00:32:02.460 --> 00:32:03.810
They look a lot alike.
They frickin' look

00:32:03.810 --> 00:32:05.330
a lock alike.

00:32:05.330 --> 00:32:07.185
Lach-alike.

00:32:07.185 --> 00:32:08.185
MacLachlans.

00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:10.393
Look at that.

00:32:12.030 --> 00:32:13.780
They do look very much alike.

00:32:13.780 --> 00:32:16.950
And so the fanny pack is more of like a--

00:32:16.950 --> 00:32:18.190
It's a crotch purse.

00:32:18.190 --> 00:32:19.023
It's a crotch cover.

00:32:19.023 --> 00:32:21.090
It looks like a bull scrotum.

00:32:21.090 --> 00:32:23.000
Well his is made of a badger.

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:24.210
And my dad's--
A badger's head.

00:32:24.210 --> 00:32:26.510
Yeah and my dad's is
made of just, you know,

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:29.363
metal and leather or something.

00:32:30.730 --> 00:32:31.900
Wow.

00:32:31.900 --> 00:32:33.960
As you can see, they
didn't hug or anything.

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:36.130
That was as close as he was
willing to get to my dad

00:32:36.130 --> 00:32:37.194
in the picture.

00:32:37.194 --> 00:32:39.400
Did he shake hands?

00:32:39.400 --> 00:32:40.700
Yeah of course.
Okay, okay.

00:32:40.700 --> 00:32:41.830
So we got a picture--
Is that the greeting,

00:32:41.830 --> 00:32:42.663
Scottish greeting?

00:32:42.663 --> 00:32:44.430
We got pictures with him.

00:32:44.430 --> 00:32:46.580
He's a swell guy.

00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:48.853
Is he a figurehead or does he do stuff?

00:32:49.690 --> 00:32:52.773
Basically at this point it's kinda like a,

00:32:54.253 --> 00:32:55.940
it's kinda like a club, essentially,

00:32:55.940 --> 00:32:57.080
you know what I'm saying?
Okay.

00:32:57.080 --> 00:32:59.490
But they--
A club.

00:32:59.490 --> 00:33:02.460
They're raising money
to restore the castle.

00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:03.917
They've done a bunch to the castle but--

00:33:03.917 --> 00:33:05.790
Did they hit you up?

00:33:05.790 --> 00:33:09.680
Well, in so many ways, yeah.

00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:11.530
He gave me a brochure
if that's what you mean.

00:33:13.940 --> 00:33:17.940
So we begin, we meet him

00:33:17.940 --> 00:33:19.990
and then we go to the old graveyard.

00:33:19.990 --> 00:33:23.220
This graveyard and there's
an old chapel that was built

00:33:23.220 --> 00:33:27.600
in the 1400s that the
Lachlans had built there,

00:33:27.600 --> 00:33:31.790
MacLachlans had built
there and then a graveyard

00:33:31.790 --> 00:33:34.370
with all these old
gravestones, we find right next

00:33:34.370 --> 00:33:37.050
to each other a Cowan which
is my mom's maiden name.

00:33:37.050 --> 00:33:37.890
What?
And a MacLachlan

00:33:37.890 --> 00:33:39.630
right next to each other
and he's like yeah,

00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:41.247
the Cowans are Scottish and so I'm--

00:33:41.247 --> 00:33:43.020
Really?
Whoa this is crazy.

00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:44.970
My mom's standing next
to the grave stones,

00:33:44.970 --> 00:33:46.950
basically about to be in tears.

00:33:46.950 --> 00:33:48.827
She's like, "Years before your daddy

00:33:48.827 --> 00:33:49.800
"and I ever got together, the Cowans

00:33:49.800 --> 00:33:51.997
"and the McLaughlins were together."

00:33:53.039 --> 00:33:56.370
And so I'm just like, I'm feeling so good

00:33:56.370 --> 00:33:57.690
about this decision.
Validated, man.

00:33:57.690 --> 00:33:59.530
I'm like I did this right, man.

00:33:59.530 --> 00:34:01.110
Yeah!
Like everybody's coming up

00:34:01.110 --> 00:34:03.070
to me about how great a
time they're having and--

00:34:03.070 --> 00:34:04.650
Yes!
And it's just,

00:34:04.650 --> 00:34:06.050
everything is going so well.

00:34:06.050 --> 00:34:07.860
What about the group photo?

00:34:07.860 --> 00:34:09.050
Did that work too?

00:34:09.050 --> 00:34:10.200
Yeah.

00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:12.482
'Cause that's the moment right
there when you say cheese.

00:34:12.482 --> 00:34:14.950
We got many, many group
photos which actually

00:34:14.950 --> 00:34:16.500
I don't have those on my
phone 'cause they're--

00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:17.340
Did you get some

00:34:17.340 --> 00:34:19.080
of just your parents?
We'll show them.

00:34:19.080 --> 00:34:20.420
Yeah, dude.
And did you get some

00:34:20.420 --> 00:34:22.783
of just your brother's family?
Yeah.

00:34:22.783 --> 00:34:24.730
Just like at a wedding,
some of just your family?

00:34:24.730 --> 00:34:26.240
All kinds--
And then some of everybody?

00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:27.120
Lots of different combinations.

00:34:27.120 --> 00:34:28.400
Yes!
Just the older boys,

00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:30.010
just the guys, just the girls.

00:34:30.010 --> 00:34:31.750
You started thinking like--
Jumping up in the air.

00:34:31.750 --> 00:34:34.180
When people start dying,
these are the photos

00:34:34.180 --> 00:34:36.091
that we'll show at the funeral type stuff.

00:34:36.091 --> 00:34:37.331
Well some of them.
Yeah.

00:34:37.331 --> 00:34:39.630
So we did some with the old
castle in the background,

00:34:39.630 --> 00:34:41.440
then we did some with the
new castle in the background

00:34:41.440 --> 00:34:43.610
and then--
Shoot different ways.

00:34:43.610 --> 00:34:44.520
Get a silhouette.

00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:47.083
We walked to the old castle, oh there's--

00:34:47.083 --> 00:34:49.060
Yes!
That's,

00:34:49.060 --> 00:34:50.300
Jenna's going through some.
Frickin' water,

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:51.370
is that the moat?

00:34:51.370 --> 00:34:55.960
That's the loch so Loch Fern is the,

00:34:55.960 --> 00:35:00.960
it's the longest sea loch in
the entire nation of Scotland.

00:35:01.120 --> 00:35:03.910
So that means that that
eventually opens up to the ocean

00:35:03.910 --> 00:35:04.930
but it's a very long,

00:35:04.930 --> 00:35:07.380
the lochs are absolutely
amazing, beautiful.

00:35:07.380 --> 00:35:08.740
This one goes all the way up.

00:35:08.740 --> 00:35:10.250
Now what's under the kilts?

00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:11.640
Nothing?

00:35:11.640 --> 00:35:14.170
So I did say that I
would be wearing nothing

00:35:14.170 --> 00:35:17.410
but then the rental
agreement stated very clearly

00:35:17.410 --> 00:35:20.650
that you had to wear underwear
underneath these kilts.

00:35:20.650 --> 00:35:21.483
Yeah but how are they gonna know?

00:35:21.483 --> 00:35:22.680
So we didn't.

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:24.970
They gonna lift the kilt
before you return it?

00:35:24.970 --> 00:35:27.180
No I did, there was lots of talk,

00:35:27.180 --> 00:35:30.140
there was lots of confident
talk about not wearing underwear

00:35:30.140 --> 00:35:32.060
but then everybody ended
up wearing underwear.

00:35:32.060 --> 00:35:33.640
Mm-hmm, well it's wool.
Most of it was

00:35:33.640 --> 00:35:35.990
we had to help each other put them on.

00:35:35.990 --> 00:35:36.823
You know what I'm saying,

00:35:36.823 --> 00:35:38.650
we were helping each other put them on.

00:35:38.650 --> 00:35:40.000
Fastening them and you don't have

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.813
to be sitting there naked before that.

00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:44.770
So anyway--
Speak for yourself.

00:35:44.770 --> 00:35:47.940
There's lots of great photos happening.

00:35:47.940 --> 00:35:49.690
Everybody's having a
great time and again--

00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:50.730
People jumping in photos.

00:35:50.730 --> 00:35:52.400
I emphasize the weather--

00:35:52.400 --> 00:35:54.563
Gotta watch the come down
with the kilt on the jump.

00:35:54.563 --> 00:35:57.930
I don't think I can, I may
sound crazy that I'm talking

00:35:57.930 --> 00:35:59.873
about the weather so much but listen,

00:35:59.873 --> 00:36:02.750
it was supposed to rain and
it rains all the time there

00:36:02.750 --> 00:36:05.240
and it was literally
supposed to rain all day

00:36:05.240 --> 00:36:07.320
and look at the weather that
we got for these photos.

00:36:07.320 --> 00:36:09.410
Perfect, perfect.
And it just kept going

00:36:09.410 --> 00:36:12.040
and going and going,
there's a cloud in the sky

00:36:12.040 --> 00:36:13.040
but not a rain drop.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:16.230
So then we go to the old castle,

00:36:16.230 --> 00:36:17.630
which all this is very
close to each other.

00:36:17.630 --> 00:36:19.460
You can see it all and
you can walk right around

00:36:19.460 --> 00:36:21.503
the end of this, right around the bay.

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:24.750
Which is a little bit of a walk for my mom

00:36:24.750 --> 00:36:26.393
but nothing too difficult.

00:36:27.890 --> 00:36:29.870
So we get to told castle

00:36:29.870 --> 00:36:32.330
and that's where I took
my sorta epic photo

00:36:32.330 --> 00:36:34.230
that I posted to Instagram.

00:36:34.230 --> 00:36:36.010
Actually my wife took that photo,

00:36:36.010 --> 00:36:38.820
not Paul the photographer
because I posted that before

00:36:38.820 --> 00:36:40.070
I got Paul's photos back.

00:36:42.239 --> 00:36:46.360
But that was the moment where
we were just kinda getting,

00:36:46.360 --> 00:36:48.160
here we are at the old castle.

00:36:48.160 --> 00:36:49.970
This thing's been here
for thousands of years.

00:36:49.970 --> 00:36:53.480
We've got the guy telling
us, he's telling us all about

00:36:53.480 --> 00:36:54.700
the history of the castle

00:36:54.700 --> 00:36:57.200
and how powerful this family used to be

00:36:57.200 --> 00:37:00.060
and the MacLachlans basically
controlled both sides

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:03.043
of the loch and it was
a powerful family and,

00:37:04.530 --> 00:37:05.930
now--

00:37:05.930 --> 00:37:06.930
Could do anything.

00:37:08.050 --> 00:37:12.099
Again, repeatedly my mom
is coming up and saying,

00:37:12.099 --> 00:37:15.000
"I couldn't have done
this without working out."

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:16.860
She said it more times than she needed to.

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:19.080
Now based on what I'm about to tell you,

00:37:19.080 --> 00:37:21.010
I wish she hadn't said it at all.

00:37:21.010 --> 00:37:23.730
But so,

00:37:23.730 --> 00:37:27.158
we walk around the castle
and we get all the pictures

00:37:27.158 --> 00:37:31.140
and then, and this is,
it's a little treacherous

00:37:31.140 --> 00:37:33.683
around the castle.

00:37:33.683 --> 00:37:35.750
It had been raining, it's always raining

00:37:35.750 --> 00:37:37.270
so it's a little bit slick in places

00:37:37.270 --> 00:37:40.307
and so there's like places
that were helping her step down

00:37:40.307 --> 00:37:43.530
and that kinda thing and then,

00:37:43.530 --> 00:37:45.740
we get up to, we've
gotten all the pictures

00:37:45.740 --> 00:37:47.370
and it's time to go.

00:37:47.370 --> 00:37:49.140
We have reservation at the restaurant

00:37:49.140 --> 00:37:51.540
which is the Inver Restaurant
which is right there next

00:37:51.540 --> 00:37:52.913
to the new castle.

00:37:54.450 --> 00:37:56.523
By the way, incredible restaurant.

00:37:58.010 --> 00:37:59.330
Like award winning.

00:37:59.330 --> 00:38:00.580
I was like everything's
going really great.

00:38:00.580 --> 00:38:02.246
We're gonna take these pictures,

00:38:02.246 --> 00:38:03.643
we're gonna have this amazing meal.

00:38:05.290 --> 00:38:09.870
And then, somebody somehow
it gets communicated

00:38:09.870 --> 00:38:13.720
that hey, go around this way,
this is the easier way out

00:38:13.720 --> 00:38:15.300
than the way that we came in.

00:38:15.300 --> 00:38:18.210
Like you got a castle that's
kind of on a peninsula.

00:38:18.210 --> 00:38:19.790
You got a path that comes up to it,

00:38:19.790 --> 00:38:21.360
then you have a path that goes around it.

00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:25.060
We had come around it all the way.

00:38:25.060 --> 00:38:27.050
So my mom is on the outside of the castle,

00:38:27.050 --> 00:38:28.430
in between the castle and the water

00:38:28.430 --> 00:38:30.080
and now we gotta go back.

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:33.593
So somehow it gets communicated
that this is the easier way.

00:38:34.930 --> 00:38:37.750
But and so my brother is with my mom

00:38:37.750 --> 00:38:39.890
and then my dad and then there's me

00:38:39.890 --> 00:38:41.960
and then everybody else and we're walking.

00:38:41.960 --> 00:38:43.960
I'm actually kinda filming some of this.

00:38:45.670 --> 00:38:48.230
But then we get down to
the side of the castle

00:38:48.230 --> 00:38:51.610
and it looks like, man,
these are like rock steps

00:38:51.610 --> 00:38:54.150
that it's kinda uneven
and this doesn't seem like

00:38:54.150 --> 00:38:56.053
it would be the easier way.

00:38:57.320 --> 00:38:58.677
And we're like, my mom was like,

00:38:58.677 --> 00:39:00.170
"This doesn't seem like the easier way."

00:39:00.170 --> 00:39:01.997
I'm like, "Yeah, it doesn't
seem like the easy way

00:39:01.997 --> 00:39:04.646
"but they said it's the easier way,"

00:39:04.646 --> 00:39:06.398
and we're kinda like, just,

00:39:06.398 --> 00:39:08.523
yeah, you're almost there anyway.

00:39:11.150 --> 00:39:14.850
So she starts taking
a couple of steps down

00:39:14.850 --> 00:39:19.584
and she gets to sort of right
on the side of the castle

00:39:19.584 --> 00:39:23.200
and at this point, my brother
and my dad and I are all,

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.499
it's kinda hitting us that

00:39:25.499 --> 00:39:27.840
there's been some miscommunication.

00:39:27.840 --> 00:39:29.573
This isn't the easier way.

00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:32.163
Turns out later what we realized is that

00:39:32.163 --> 00:39:35.990
what the chairman had told us
is that this is the easier way

00:39:35.990 --> 00:39:37.887
to see this side of
the castle or something

00:39:37.887 --> 00:39:41.480
and it got through 12 people
through the grapevine,

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:42.570
somehow it got communicated

00:39:42.570 --> 00:39:44.510
that this was the easier way back.

00:39:44.510 --> 00:39:46.160
Mm-hmm.
And then she was basically

00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:48.713
already almost all the way through it.

00:39:50.240 --> 00:39:54.030
And who, who's to blame?

00:39:54.030 --> 00:39:57.170
I mean, me, my brother, my dad.

00:39:57.170 --> 00:39:59.730
We're all to blame and
I think at this point,

00:39:59.730 --> 00:40:00.910
we're all just taking--
I wasn't there.

00:40:00.910 --> 00:40:02.850
We're all just taking the blame equally.

00:40:02.850 --> 00:40:04.230
Okay.
Even though my brother

00:40:04.230 --> 00:40:06.610
was the one who was in
the lead and he is the one

00:40:06.610 --> 00:40:09.170
that is taking the blame more than me,

00:40:09.170 --> 00:40:12.570
which we're all just
like, this was a mistake.

00:40:12.570 --> 00:40:15.867
Someone should have sounded
the alarm and should have said,

00:40:15.867 --> 00:40:17.337
"This is not the best way.

00:40:17.337 --> 00:40:19.580
"This is not the easiest
way, let's go back around."

00:40:19.580 --> 00:40:20.553
But none of us did.

00:40:21.650 --> 00:40:22.750
So we're all to blame.

00:40:24.546 --> 00:40:26.570
But--
For what exactly?

00:40:26.570 --> 00:40:29.040
I turned my camera off 'cause I was like

00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:32.210
I gotta get down here,
I gotta spot my mom.

00:40:32.210 --> 00:40:34.530
'Cause I got my dad and my
brother there and I'm like,

00:40:34.530 --> 00:40:37.920
if she misses a step, she
could fall into the loch,

00:40:37.920 --> 00:40:42.060
so I get down there and I'm
like on the rocks like spotting.

00:40:42.060 --> 00:40:43.080
Okay.

00:40:43.080 --> 00:40:46.480
And then there was like one more step

00:40:47.350 --> 00:40:50.103
to get down to basically be on dirt.

00:40:51.220 --> 00:40:52.650
I'm like she's gonna do this.

00:40:52.650 --> 00:40:53.650
She's gonna make it.

00:40:55.010 --> 00:40:56.723
She takes this one step.

00:40:58.300 --> 00:40:59.333
Lost her foot.

00:41:01.610 --> 00:41:06.610
Falls down, her legs sort
of buckle underneath her

00:41:06.710 --> 00:41:09.817
and then she immediately
begins screaming and she says,

00:41:09.817 --> 00:41:11.380
"I broke my leg!"

00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:12.333
Oh no!

00:41:14.089 --> 00:41:14.922
Oh no!

00:41:15.940 --> 00:41:18.930
And so I look down expect--
She's screaming.

00:41:18.930 --> 00:41:20.228
I broke my leg!

00:41:20.228 --> 00:41:21.400
And basically cry--
Oh no.

00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:23.235
Crying, she's crying.

00:41:23.235 --> 00:41:24.350
On my last step.

00:41:24.350 --> 00:41:27.310
And so 50 things go through my mind.

00:41:27.310 --> 00:41:28.700
The first thing is I'm gonna look down

00:41:28.700 --> 00:41:31.810
and see a compound fracture and
see my mom's bone coming out

00:41:31.810 --> 00:41:33.760
of her leg and I don't see that

00:41:33.760 --> 00:41:35.260
and I'm immediately like okay,

00:41:36.977 --> 00:41:38.603
maybe she didn't break her leg.

00:41:39.690 --> 00:41:42.920
But I do see her, one
of her ankles is kinda,

00:41:42.920 --> 00:41:45.426
it's kind of in an awkward angle.

00:41:45.426 --> 00:41:46.480
Okay.

00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:48.833
But we immediately begin to get her and,

00:41:50.549 --> 00:41:53.863
second thing I'm thinking is,
if she has broken her leg,

00:41:55.510 --> 00:41:57.780
how in the hell are we
gonna get her out of here?

00:41:57.780 --> 00:42:01.053
We're like way out in
this place where you have

00:42:01.053 --> 00:42:03.260
to come down this dirt road and--

00:42:03.260 --> 00:42:04.093
Build a raft!

00:42:04.093 --> 00:42:05.750
We're gonna float her down the loch!

00:42:05.750 --> 00:42:07.830
And then we had to go
down this little path

00:42:07.830 --> 00:42:10.310
and then there's these rocks and--

00:42:10.310 --> 00:42:11.620
Everybody take off their kilt,

00:42:11.620 --> 00:42:13.641
we're gonna make a parachute!

00:42:13.641 --> 00:42:15.680
And so, I think we're all kinda thinking,

00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:17.930
we gotta get her up
and get her out of here

00:42:17.930 --> 00:42:22.650
so I'm like you know what,
let's just stand you up

00:42:22.650 --> 00:42:25.067
so we stand her up and she's like ,

00:42:26.114 --> 00:42:28.600
"It really hurts, it really
hurts, really hurts."

00:42:28.600 --> 00:42:32.157
And I'm like, "Okay, but can
you, with us kinda helping you,

00:42:32.157 --> 00:42:35.247
"can you walk out of here?

00:42:35.247 --> 00:42:37.923
"Because we really need
you to walk out of here."

00:42:39.670 --> 00:42:42.890
So she takes some very labored steps,

00:42:42.890 --> 00:42:45.470
putting most of her weight
on us but she's kind

00:42:45.470 --> 00:42:49.144
of putting equal weight on both feet

00:42:49.144 --> 00:42:51.457
and then we talked to
the chairman who says,

00:42:51.457 --> 00:42:53.307
"I'll drive my car up here to the place

00:42:53.307 --> 00:42:55.580
"you can get the car the closest."

00:42:55.580 --> 00:42:57.910
She's a Cowan, they
married the MacLachlans.

00:42:57.910 --> 00:42:59.870
And so as she's walking--

00:42:59.870 --> 00:43:02.430
Hard, hardened people.
As she's walking,

00:43:02.430 --> 00:43:03.830
we're kinda talking amongst ourselves

00:43:03.830 --> 00:43:06.220
and we're kinda like a
few feet away from her.

00:43:06.220 --> 00:43:10.647
My brother and my dad have
her and then Jessie was like,

00:43:10.647 --> 00:43:12.248
"She's putting a lot of weight on it,

00:43:12.248 --> 00:43:15.057
"maybe it's not broken," and
then the nephews are like,

00:43:15.057 --> 00:43:17.030
"It's not broken, it's not broken."

00:43:17.030 --> 00:43:18.330
Everybody's like, "It's not broken."

00:43:18.330 --> 00:43:22.951
She turned it, she may actually
be in shock at this point.

00:43:22.951 --> 00:43:26.199
Let's just get her to the restaurant

00:43:26.199 --> 00:43:29.000
'cause we got this
reservation at the restaurant

00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:31.366
and let's elevate her foot, you know,

00:43:31.366 --> 00:43:34.510
give her some pain reliever.
Yeah.

00:43:34.510 --> 00:43:36.500
And hope for the best.

00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:38.423
Right, I mean you can turn your ankle,

00:43:39.461 --> 00:43:41.386
it can hurt pretty bad.

00:43:41.386 --> 00:43:43.950
So we do, we get her to the restaurant.

00:43:43.950 --> 00:43:47.664
We elevate her ankle, give
her some pain reliever.

00:43:47.664 --> 00:43:48.593
Ice it?

00:43:49.874 --> 00:43:53.220
We did not ice it because,

00:43:53.220 --> 00:43:56.260
you know how Locke is like mister expert

00:43:56.260 --> 00:43:57.700
about lots of things?

00:43:57.700 --> 00:43:59.770
He gets it from the best.

00:43:59.770 --> 00:44:04.770
And so with a sprained ankle,
the latest research apparently

00:44:05.320 --> 00:44:07.840
is that the immediate
icing is not actually

00:44:07.840 --> 00:44:10.350
what you're supposed to do with a sprain.

00:44:10.350 --> 00:44:12.460
I don't know whether he's right or wrong.

00:44:12.460 --> 00:44:14.460
Elevation is definitely a good thing

00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:17.645
so we were like, all
right, let's just do this

00:44:17.645 --> 00:44:19.670
and have a good meal.

00:44:19.670 --> 00:44:21.390
I mean Locke did know about the website

00:44:21.390 --> 00:44:22.430
where you could take the size--

00:44:22.430 --> 00:44:23.263
He did--
The size of continents

00:44:23.263 --> 00:44:25.551
and put them over other countries and--

00:44:25.551 --> 00:44:30.390
So we have a great meal
and I think we've all kinda

00:44:30.390 --> 00:44:32.830
just talked ourselves into, yeah,

00:44:32.830 --> 00:44:34.090
maybe she sprained it or whatever.

00:44:34.090 --> 00:44:38.210
Now she's saying, "I
need to go to a doctor."

00:44:38.210 --> 00:44:40.150
And we're just like,
don't wanna have to deal

00:44:40.150 --> 00:44:42.331
with taking her to a doctor.

00:44:42.331 --> 00:44:43.231
Where we gonna go?

00:44:44.525 --> 00:44:45.470
We just don't wanna face,

00:44:45.470 --> 00:44:47.700
we don't wanna face
that potential reality.

00:44:47.700 --> 00:44:49.230
Right.

00:44:49.230 --> 00:44:51.080
So--
And it's not your ankle.

00:44:51.080 --> 00:44:52.690
Right, come on.

00:44:52.690 --> 00:44:55.650
So now, it hasn't rained this whole day

00:44:55.650 --> 00:44:56.970
but it's supposed to rain--
You don't wanna face

00:44:56.970 --> 00:44:58.320
that reality, I get it.

00:44:58.320 --> 00:45:01.351
And it looks like the rain
clouds are really coming in

00:45:01.351 --> 00:45:04.670
and then I'm like, we need
to get her into the car.

00:45:04.670 --> 00:45:06.580
We need to get home to the hotel

00:45:06.580 --> 00:45:08.630
and then we kinda need to regroup.

00:45:08.630 --> 00:45:10.470
Now keep in mind we're
like an hour and a half

00:45:10.470 --> 00:45:12.880
or so away from where we were staying.

00:45:12.880 --> 00:45:14.000
Oh.

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:17.180
So we get her into the
car which was not easy,

00:45:17.180 --> 00:45:19.963
had to take her down the steps.

00:45:21.201 --> 00:45:23.534
It ended up being that Jessie

00:45:23.534 --> 00:45:26.020
and my dad were the two
best people to do this.

00:45:26.020 --> 00:45:27.370
I'm too tall.

00:45:27.370 --> 00:45:30.310
She needs to put her arms
on someone's shoulders

00:45:30.310 --> 00:45:32.420
and I'm so much bigger
than her that like--

00:45:32.420 --> 00:45:34.410
You're less of a crutch
and more of a crane.

00:45:34.410 --> 00:45:36.500
Yeah and so Jessie's the perfect height

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:39.440
for her to do that and my dad is 5'9"

00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:40.763
so he's able to get down.

00:45:42.270 --> 00:45:43.500
So they get her to the car.

00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:44.780
Plus you need to film it.

00:45:44.780 --> 00:45:46.890
Yeah and I didn't film a lot of this.

00:45:46.890 --> 00:45:48.400
I will say, I felt bad.

00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:51.750
So we get her in the
car and I'm not kidding,

00:45:51.750 --> 00:45:54.850
two minutes later it just
starts pouring down rain.

00:45:54.850 --> 00:45:56.810
I was like oh gosh, I'm so glad we got her

00:45:56.810 --> 00:45:58.760
into the car before this
happened because this would have

00:45:58.760 --> 00:46:01.130
really complicated things.
Mm-hmm.

00:46:01.130 --> 00:46:04.840
We start driving back, now,
she's in my brother's car,

00:46:04.840 --> 00:46:05.890
the van he's driving.

00:46:07.120 --> 00:46:11.393
And so I'm driving along and we get up to,

00:46:12.280 --> 00:46:13.520
we're following the road
and all of a sudden,

00:46:13.520 --> 00:46:14.730
there's a bunch of cars stopped

00:46:14.730 --> 00:46:19.330
and this woman says, tells
us to roll down the window

00:46:19.330 --> 00:46:20.163
and she's like,

00:46:22.427 --> 00:46:24.990
"The river's bursted."

00:46:24.990 --> 00:46:25.823
What?

00:46:25.823 --> 00:46:27.680
"The river's bursted the road."

00:46:27.680 --> 00:46:29.350
The river's bursted.

00:46:29.350 --> 00:46:33.820
Yeah and I look down and
I see just this torrent

00:46:33.820 --> 00:46:36.880
of water just barreling across the road,

00:46:36.880 --> 00:46:41.240
carrying large things across the road.

00:46:41.240 --> 00:46:43.030
Everybody take off your kilt!

00:46:43.030 --> 00:46:44.800
We're gonna build a raft!

00:46:44.800 --> 00:46:48.146
And I'm like okay, so
I'm like, "Okay, well,

00:46:48.146 --> 00:46:51.050
"there's another way out of this place."

00:46:51.050 --> 00:46:53.899
You could just get up a lot of speed.

00:46:53.899 --> 00:46:55.430
Vroom!
So I turned around

00:46:55.430 --> 00:46:57.667
and then get the map out and start looking

00:46:57.667 --> 00:46:59.710
and quickly realize that no,

00:46:59.710 --> 00:47:02.134
this is the only way out of this place.

00:47:02.134 --> 00:47:02.967
What?

00:47:02.967 --> 00:47:03.910
There is no other road.

00:47:03.910 --> 00:47:07.123
It literally is this or take a boat.

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:13.244
So Cole and I go back, at
this point I'm beginning

00:47:13.244 --> 00:47:15.360
to get a little panicked because I'm like,

00:47:15.360 --> 00:47:17.460
my mom needs to get back to her stuff.

00:47:17.460 --> 00:47:18.860
She's got like her medication

00:47:18.860 --> 00:47:22.920
and I don't know what the
deal is with her ankle

00:47:22.920 --> 00:47:26.382
but it's starting to get
dark in a little bit.

00:47:26.382 --> 00:47:28.110
This is late in the afternoon

00:47:29.021 --> 00:47:34.021
and we go into this little
local pub and hotel area

00:47:34.630 --> 00:47:36.527
and we're just like,
"What do you guys think?

00:47:36.527 --> 00:47:38.997
"We gotta get back to
here," and they're like,

00:47:38.997 --> 00:47:42.110
"Oh, you're gonna have to take the ferry."

00:47:42.110 --> 00:47:44.223
I'm like what, we have to take a ferry?

00:47:45.600 --> 00:47:48.770
I got a woman that can't
get anywhere right now

00:47:48.770 --> 00:47:51.090
and I got 12 people in two vans.

00:47:51.090 --> 00:47:53.410
It's no ferry involved here.

00:47:53.410 --> 00:47:55.830
Did I mention I'm an internet celebrity?

00:47:55.830 --> 00:47:57.500
Did you think about pulling that card?

00:47:57.500 --> 00:48:00.180
No and they're like, "You
can stay here tonight."

00:48:00.180 --> 00:48:01.490
Oh what, okay.

00:48:01.490 --> 00:48:03.340
Turns out they had two
rooms which would not

00:48:03.340 --> 00:48:06.180
have gone over well.

00:48:06.180 --> 00:48:08.300
But 'cause I was like we got 12 people

00:48:08.300 --> 00:48:11.037
and so then they're like,
"The best thing to do

00:48:11.037 --> 00:48:12.367
"is just wait it out.

00:48:12.367 --> 00:48:13.447
"You should probably just wait it out

00:48:13.447 --> 00:48:15.340
"and eventually the road will clear up,"

00:48:15.340 --> 00:48:17.047
but then a guy comes down and says,

00:48:17.047 --> 00:48:19.427
"There's giant boulders
and trees on the road

00:48:19.427 --> 00:48:23.224
"and the estimate is that it
will take six hours to clear."

00:48:23.224 --> 00:48:24.057
What?

00:48:24.057 --> 00:48:26.837
"So you've gotta take the ferry."

00:48:28.100 --> 00:48:31.360
So I don't think I do very
well in these situations.

00:48:31.360 --> 00:48:33.075
I think I did okay.

00:48:33.075 --> 00:48:36.060
I don't think I panicked
too much and I kept saying,

00:48:36.060 --> 00:48:38.052
I was telling Jessie, I was like,

00:48:38.052 --> 00:48:41.597
"If Mama Di," that's what we call her,

00:48:41.597 --> 00:48:43.921
"If Mama Di didn't have
this ankle situation--"

00:48:43.921 --> 00:48:45.687
I thought you said, "If mama dies,

00:48:45.687 --> 00:48:47.459
"this is what we're gonna do."

00:48:47.459 --> 00:48:49.520
No, Diane is her name, Mama Di,

00:48:49.520 --> 00:48:50.837
that's what all the grandkids call her.

00:48:51.960 --> 00:48:54.960
So if Mama Di was not in this situation,

00:48:54.960 --> 00:48:56.370
this would be a bit of an adventure,

00:48:56.370 --> 00:49:00.210
stuck on a peninsula in Scotland
and having to take a ferry

00:49:00.210 --> 00:49:04.550
to get back home but because
she's in this state--

00:49:04.550 --> 00:49:07.240
For her it's not, but
it can still be for us.

00:49:07.240 --> 00:49:09.070
I feel pretty bad.
Okay yeah.

00:49:09.070 --> 00:49:12.120
So we, turns out the ferry
is one of those ferries

00:49:12.120 --> 00:49:13.800
you can drive your van onto.

00:49:13.800 --> 00:49:15.621
That's what I thought all along, man.

00:49:15.621 --> 00:49:20.621
Okay so we go down and we
get the next to last ferry

00:49:21.680 --> 00:49:22.930
for the day.
Oh nice.

00:49:22.930 --> 00:49:26.610
It takes us across a loch

00:49:26.610 --> 00:49:29.193
to almost all the way to Glasgow.

00:49:32.037 --> 00:49:35.260
It took us a long time, we
added like almost two hours

00:49:35.260 --> 00:49:36.710
to our trip to get back home.

00:49:37.900 --> 00:49:39.880
And I call ahead of time
to the place, I'm like,

00:49:39.880 --> 00:49:42.880
'cause there's no elevator
to the first floor.

00:49:42.880 --> 00:49:45.510
The first floor in the UK
means the second floor.

00:49:45.510 --> 00:49:47.310
Ground floor means ground floor.

00:49:47.310 --> 00:49:50.350
First floor is the one above
it, and there's only stairs,

00:49:50.350 --> 00:49:53.980
stairs that kinda go, this was
kind of a pretty rustic place

00:49:53.980 --> 00:49:57.020
were were staying in Glencoe
'cause everything's rustic.

00:49:57.020 --> 00:49:59.657
Like call ahead and say,
"Is there a way to get there

00:49:59.657 --> 00:50:02.127
"more easily, like a
luggage lift or whatever?"

00:50:03.220 --> 00:50:05.540
You gonna put her in a--

00:50:05.540 --> 00:50:07.160
Yeah.
In a dinghy?

00:50:07.160 --> 00:50:09.100
What's that thing called where the--

00:50:09.100 --> 00:50:12.140
Well not one of those, it
would have been electric.

00:50:12.140 --> 00:50:14.970
But there was a fire
escape that has just like

00:50:14.970 --> 00:50:17.793
two steps that she can
use so we go to that,

00:50:18.740 --> 00:50:20.735
we get her into bed that night

00:50:20.735 --> 00:50:23.660
and we kinda take a picture of the ankle

00:50:23.660 --> 00:50:26.190
and send it to a doctor friend.

00:50:26.190 --> 00:50:27.023
The doctor friend is like,

00:50:27.023 --> 00:50:28.876
"Yeah, you should get that looked at."

00:50:28.876 --> 00:50:31.810
So that was when I was on the phone

00:50:31.810 --> 00:50:36.350
with Jenna who at the
time was at Disneyland.

00:50:36.350 --> 00:50:37.183
Gah!

00:50:37.183 --> 00:50:38.073
I ruined her day.

00:50:39.380 --> 00:50:43.430
And you know, interestingly my brother

00:50:43.430 --> 00:50:46.452
and Jenna both independently found a place

00:50:46.452 --> 00:50:49.830
that was close by that specialize,

00:50:49.830 --> 00:50:52.060
it said it specializes
in mountain injuries.

00:50:52.060 --> 00:50:52.893
Ah.
You know,

00:50:52.893 --> 00:50:53.726
'cause we're in the mountains

00:50:53.726 --> 00:50:55.710
and apparently people get injured.

00:50:55.710 --> 00:50:58.380
And so the first thing
in that next morning,

00:50:58.380 --> 00:51:03.210
we take her to this hospital

00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:05.620
and shout-out to socialized medicine

00:51:05.620 --> 00:51:09.650
because it was completely
free, even for Americans.

00:51:09.650 --> 00:51:11.340
It's free for anyone--
Really.

00:51:11.340 --> 00:51:14.400
Who gets their stuff looked at.

00:51:14.400 --> 00:51:16.970
And what was your mom's
disposition going to bed

00:51:16.970 --> 00:51:19.050
the night before and
then the next morning?

00:51:19.050 --> 00:51:21.243
She was actually in really good spirits.

00:51:22.830 --> 00:51:25.510
She felt bad but we were like listen,

00:51:25.510 --> 00:51:26.690
it ain't your fault, it's our fault.

00:51:26.690 --> 00:51:29.040
We're the ones who led you down this path.

00:51:29.040 --> 00:51:29.873
Literally.

00:51:29.873 --> 00:51:32.810
And you know what, there are
only a couple more days here

00:51:32.810 --> 00:51:37.090
that, basically all the
major stuff, we've done it.

00:51:37.090 --> 00:51:38.493
We got all the pictures.

00:51:40.500 --> 00:51:41.940
We're gonna just take
you to this hospital,

00:51:41.940 --> 00:51:43.610
get you looked at.
If you lose a foot now,

00:51:43.610 --> 00:51:45.230
you'll have 'em in the photos.

00:51:45.230 --> 00:51:48.659
And I was just thinking,
okay, we're gonna go

00:51:48.659 --> 00:51:51.490
to this place and the
doctor's gonna be like,

00:51:51.490 --> 00:51:53.330
oh it's a sprain--
Wrap it.

00:51:53.330 --> 00:51:55.137
Let me wrap it in something
and then just give her,

00:51:55.137 --> 00:51:58.540
you know, just give her some
prescription painkillers

00:51:58.540 --> 00:52:00.590
or something, I don't know.

00:52:00.590 --> 00:52:03.350
And actually I ended
up, so Cole and my dad

00:52:03.350 --> 00:52:05.270
and Jessie took her to that and then I had

00:52:05.270 --> 00:52:08.235
to take all the kilts back to the place

00:52:08.235 --> 00:52:10.980
and so we kinda separated for that.

00:52:10.980 --> 00:52:12.210
It's like what are 12 people gonna do,

00:52:12.210 --> 00:52:13.210
sit around and wait.

00:52:14.570 --> 00:52:17.960
But we get a text.

00:52:17.960 --> 00:52:20.760
We get a text from Micah, my nephew.

00:52:20.760 --> 00:52:22.820
No Micah's with me, he gets a text,

00:52:22.820 --> 00:52:24.910
'cause he was the one that
was checking his phone first

00:52:24.910 --> 00:52:26.580
when we were out and

00:52:28.640 --> 00:52:32.080
the ankle is broken.

00:52:32.080 --> 00:52:33.663
In four places.
What?

00:52:35.013 --> 00:52:37.640
Four places?

00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:39.340
Yeah.
How,

00:52:39.340 --> 00:52:41.730
I didn't even know an
ankle had four places.

00:52:41.730 --> 00:52:43.070
Ankle's got lots of places, man.

00:52:43.070 --> 00:52:44.180
What?
At least four

00:52:44.180 --> 00:52:45.130
that you can break.

00:52:47.030 --> 00:52:50.690
And first of all, you know,

00:52:50.690 --> 00:52:52.690
my mom was in really good spirits.

00:52:52.690 --> 00:52:57.030
She really liked this
doctor who was like funny,

00:52:57.030 --> 00:53:00.293
spent like five hours with them.

00:53:01.200 --> 00:53:04.137
Of course he did the x-ray and then he--

00:53:04.137 --> 00:53:06.060
Are you sure he didn't break her ankle

00:53:06.060 --> 00:53:07.490
in a couple of places?
And then he put her

00:53:07.490 --> 00:53:10.480
in a cast but then he
x-rayed it after the cast

00:53:10.480 --> 00:53:11.930
and he wasn't happy
with the way that it set

00:53:11.930 --> 00:53:13.570
so we took it off and did it again

00:53:13.570 --> 00:53:15.180
and got it set just right.

00:53:15.180 --> 00:53:17.440
Gave her some laughing
gas, she had a great time.

00:53:17.440 --> 00:53:19.225
Oh yeah she did.

00:53:19.225 --> 00:53:20.760
And again this was all free.

00:53:20.760 --> 00:53:23.943
They'd hardly had to wait and
the guy was super competent.

00:53:25.520 --> 00:53:26.690
Gave her laughing gas.

00:53:26.690 --> 00:53:29.597
And but then he's basically like,

00:53:29.597 --> 00:53:32.237
"As soon as you get back to the US,

00:53:32.237 --> 00:53:35.817
"you need to present
yourself in an emergency room

00:53:35.817 --> 00:53:37.377
"because you're not gonna be
able to get an appointment

00:53:37.377 --> 00:53:38.650
"with an orthopedist."

00:53:38.650 --> 00:53:40.620
I thought you were gonna say,
you need to present yourself

00:53:40.620 --> 00:53:44.335
to a lawyer and take
your son out of the will.

00:53:44.335 --> 00:53:46.827
And he's like, "You need
to go to an emergency room

00:53:46.827 --> 00:53:49.067
"'cause this is an emergency
and they're likely going

00:53:49.067 --> 00:53:51.540
"to want to," because
she's not very mobile

00:53:51.540 --> 00:53:54.520
and that other leg is
not very strong so she,

00:53:54.520 --> 00:53:57.340
it's really hard for her to
not put any weight on it.

00:53:57.340 --> 00:54:00.150
She's basically immobile at this point.

00:54:00.150 --> 00:54:00.983
Mm-hmm.

00:54:00.983 --> 00:54:02.977
Can't put any weight on it and he's like,

00:54:02.977 --> 00:54:04.797
"You need to get somebody to look at it.

00:54:04.797 --> 00:54:06.297
"They're most likely
gonna have to do surgery

00:54:06.297 --> 00:54:09.450
"to get a plate and some
screws and a plate installed--"

00:54:09.450 --> 00:54:10.283
Good God.
Because that's what you

00:54:10.283 --> 00:54:13.410
have to do when someone
is inevitably gonna put

00:54:13.410 --> 00:54:15.710
some weight on it and
it doesn't need to move.

00:54:17.931 --> 00:54:19.730
So of course at this point it's like,

00:54:19.730 --> 00:54:22.770
I just feel horrible, right,

00:54:22.770 --> 00:54:26.840
and whether or not, first of all, I take,

00:54:26.840 --> 00:54:31.060
I share the blame with
my brother and my dad

00:54:31.060 --> 00:54:33.633
in not stopping and not
going down this path.

00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:38.720
But I take more of the blame
because this was all my idea.

00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:42.860
You know, and I'm the one
that got her the trainer

00:54:42.860 --> 00:54:46.400
and gave her the confidence
that she could do anything,

00:54:46.400 --> 00:54:50.902
walk around this place and
now she's sitting in there,

00:54:50.902 --> 00:54:54.150
she's sitting with a cast.

00:54:54.150 --> 00:54:57.860
We go to, the last two
nights we stayed in a place

00:54:57.860 --> 00:55:00.000
called Broomhall Castle in Ministry

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.070
which outside of
Edinburgh which is an old,

00:55:02.070 --> 00:55:04.620
it's a castle that you can
stay in, it's very cool.

00:55:05.850 --> 00:55:08.560
And they thankfully, they
did have a luggage lift

00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:11.540
that was not intended for
people but was big enough

00:55:11.540 --> 00:55:13.370
for people and she was able to use that

00:55:13.370 --> 00:55:16.260
to get into her room and I
went and I rented a wheelchair

00:55:16.260 --> 00:55:18.710
from a place that you
can rent wheelchairs from

00:55:19.632 --> 00:55:21.620
and then we arranged a
whole deal about okay,

00:55:21.620 --> 00:55:23.550
well she's gonna have to
have a greeter meet her

00:55:23.550 --> 00:55:25.080
at the airport with the wheelchair

00:55:25.080 --> 00:55:26.600
and then she's gotta have
somebody help her get

00:55:26.600 --> 00:55:28.350
onto the plane and there's a special chair

00:55:28.350 --> 00:55:30.730
that you get, an aisle
wheelchair that takes you

00:55:30.730 --> 00:55:32.350
down the aisle and then
you're put into your seat

00:55:32.350 --> 00:55:34.510
'cause she's really not able
to put any weight on it.

00:55:34.510 --> 00:55:35.343
Yeah.

00:55:35.343 --> 00:55:36.410
And just very immobile.

00:55:36.410 --> 00:55:37.830
So you made all those arrangements.

00:55:37.830 --> 00:55:41.637
Made all those arrangements
and where it ended up is

00:55:41.637 --> 00:55:45.040
she was able to get an
appointment on Monday morning

00:55:45.040 --> 00:55:47.440
that she got back with an orthopedist

00:55:47.440 --> 00:55:49.630
who looked at it and said, "You
know we need to do surgery,"

00:55:49.630 --> 00:55:52.023
scheduled surgery for two days later.

00:55:53.250 --> 00:55:58.250
She got the surgery and
she's got like people

00:55:58.600 --> 00:56:03.505
from her church coming and
building a ramp for her to,

00:56:03.505 --> 00:56:07.143
the church had a wheelchair
and then they're like

00:56:07.143 --> 00:56:11.130
giving her basically a handicapped toilet

00:56:11.130 --> 00:56:15.950
with railings on the side and
stuff so everybody's kinda

00:56:15.950 --> 00:56:18.040
coming together and taking care of her

00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:22.110
but she's gonna be in this
splint as the swelling goes down

00:56:22.110 --> 00:56:23.910
for two weeks and then
I think she's in a cast

00:56:23.910 --> 00:56:27.130
for like six weeks, then she's
in a boot for four weeks.

00:56:27.130 --> 00:56:30.290
This is the next three
months of her life basically,

00:56:30.290 --> 00:56:31.840
drastically altered.

00:56:31.840 --> 00:56:35.630
My dad's time drastically altered.

00:56:35.630 --> 00:56:38.659
We got a woman who's coming
to spend all her time

00:56:38.659 --> 00:56:41.390
when my dad's not there
'cause my dad teaches law,

00:56:41.390 --> 00:56:44.320
still is teaching law.

00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:47.183
When he goes to school, we
gotta have somebody watch her.

00:56:48.250 --> 00:56:52.040
So that is the situation
now is that, again,

00:56:52.040 --> 00:56:53.373
she's in good spirits.

00:56:54.220 --> 00:56:55.930
She's gonna be fine.

00:56:55.930 --> 00:56:57.290
She's not mad at you.

00:56:57.290 --> 00:57:00.500
No, well, if she is,
she hasn't stated that.

00:57:00.500 --> 00:57:04.980
She's been very, she is not,
there's been no blame placed

00:57:04.980 --> 00:57:07.800
on any of us.

00:57:07.800 --> 00:57:12.800
But I mean obviously I
feel horrible about this

00:57:13.150 --> 00:57:16.031
'cause I'm like, all
right, now I feel like

00:57:16.031 --> 00:57:20.820
all the progress that
she made to get ready

00:57:20.820 --> 00:57:23.580
for this trip, I feel
like that's kinda undone.

00:57:23.580 --> 00:57:26.802
Because it's like no, okay
well, she's gonna have to,

00:57:26.802 --> 00:57:28.980
she's gotta go through
this recovery process

00:57:28.980 --> 00:57:31.940
which who knows how long
that'll take, I mean at her age,

00:57:31.940 --> 00:57:35.300
she may take longer to heal or whatever,

00:57:35.300 --> 00:57:37.530
there may be another setback
and I don't want this

00:57:37.530 --> 00:57:39.790
to be the beginning of
her being more immobile

00:57:39.790 --> 00:57:42.130
than she was before the trip.

00:57:42.130 --> 00:57:43.900
'Cause for me it was sort of like win-win,

00:57:43.900 --> 00:57:47.300
it was just like, you
know, she's gonna be better

00:57:47.300 --> 00:57:49.100
for this trip but this will also be a way

00:57:49.100 --> 00:57:50.500
to kinda get her into the habit.

00:57:50.500 --> 00:57:51.777
She was like, "I'm gonna
go back to my trainer

00:57:51.777 --> 00:57:53.500
"after I get back from the trip."

00:57:53.500 --> 00:57:55.730
She ain't going back to
the trainer anytime soon.

00:57:57.670 --> 00:57:59.870
So yeah, that's what happened.

00:57:59.870 --> 00:58:01.360
Well listen.

00:58:01.360 --> 00:58:04.180
It wouldn't have happened
if it weren't for you.

00:58:04.180 --> 00:58:07.147
But--

00:58:07.147 --> 00:58:07.980
Thanks, Link.
That doesn't mean

00:58:07.980 --> 00:58:08.963
that it's your fault.

00:58:10.279 --> 00:58:13.940
So I agree with everything
you're saying but also...

00:58:19.058 --> 00:58:20.770
It was an accident.

00:58:20.770 --> 00:58:25.280
Accidents happen all
the time but it happened

00:58:25.280 --> 00:58:27.660
in the context of something that also,

00:58:27.660 --> 00:58:31.710
a bunch of positive and a bunch
of positive can still come

00:58:31.710 --> 00:58:34.900
out of this that wouldn't have happened

00:58:34.900 --> 00:58:37.510
if it wasn't for you as well.

00:58:37.510 --> 00:58:41.853
So I mean she's got one hell of a story.

00:58:43.060 --> 00:58:45.210
So do you which--

00:58:45.210 --> 00:58:46.410
If you're gonna break your ankle,

00:58:46.410 --> 00:58:48.240
this is not a bad place to do it.

00:58:48.240 --> 00:58:50.520
She got a great, if you're
gonna break your ankle,

00:58:50.520 --> 00:58:52.890
you might as well have a great
story to go along with it

00:58:52.890 --> 00:58:55.300
and she's got not only a great
story but a great picture

00:58:55.300 --> 00:58:56.870
from just hours before.

00:58:56.870 --> 00:58:58.320
But this is probably a good time

00:58:58.320 --> 00:59:01.180
to tell you another key
piece of information.

00:59:01.180 --> 00:59:06.180
After all this, paying a lot of money

00:59:06.737 --> 00:59:11.737
to have the McLaughlins go
back to their ancestral home

00:59:11.940 --> 00:59:14.410
to meet the chief of the clan,

00:59:14.410 --> 00:59:18.023
to get their picture taken
at the Lachlan castle,

00:59:19.290 --> 00:59:21.930
to having my mom break her leg--

00:59:21.930 --> 00:59:24.860
In four places.
Ankle in four places

00:59:24.860 --> 00:59:29.383
at the Lachlan castle,
turns out we're Irish.

00:59:34.060 --> 00:59:34.893
We're Irish.

00:59:37.920 --> 00:59:39.010
What?

00:59:39.010 --> 00:59:42.486
What are you?

00:59:42.486 --> 00:59:44.510
What are you talking about?

00:59:44.510 --> 00:59:45.470
What do you mean?

00:59:45.470 --> 00:59:46.700
We're Irish.

00:59:46.700 --> 00:59:48.210
Yeah but--

00:59:48.210 --> 00:59:49.260
We're not Scottish.

00:59:51.200 --> 00:59:52.033
What?

00:59:53.260 --> 00:59:55.533
What do you, what happened?

00:59:57.110 --> 01:00:00.847
Well, I probably could have
done a little more research.

01:00:08.810 --> 01:00:12.423
But who did research afterward?

01:00:13.420 --> 01:00:15.333
That's the wrong time to do research.

01:00:16.370 --> 01:00:18.820
Well, I will say that I actually knew this

01:00:18.820 --> 01:00:20.253
before she broke her ankle.

01:00:22.210 --> 01:00:27.210
Because my brother picked up a pamphlet.

01:00:28.700 --> 01:00:31.671
It turns out all you gotta
do is pick up a pamphlet.

01:00:31.671 --> 01:00:33.300
What?
We were in,

01:00:33.300 --> 01:00:34.490
it was actually in Edinburgh,

01:00:34.490 --> 01:00:36.920
we were in St. John's Cathedral.

01:00:36.920 --> 01:00:39.280
Now okay, that was a great punchline.

01:00:39.280 --> 01:00:41.920
I will say, we don't--

01:00:41.920 --> 01:00:42.930
Just tell me what happened.

01:00:42.930 --> 01:00:44.710
Just tell me what's on the pamphlet.

01:00:44.710 --> 01:00:48.287
So Cole says, "Hey, in this thing

01:00:48.287 --> 01:00:50.840
"that says McLoughlin on
it," spelled with a O,

01:00:50.840 --> 01:00:53.170
kinda like how Jacksepticeye spells it

01:00:53.170 --> 01:00:56.063
which is basically
interchangeable, the O and the A.

01:00:57.110 --> 01:01:02.110
It says here that the GH
spelling is from Ireland

01:01:03.670 --> 01:01:08.670
and that some of the Irish
McLoughlins came over

01:01:08.817 --> 01:01:12.443
many years ago and became the MacLachlans.

01:01:14.253 --> 01:01:19.253
And so the MacLachlans,
if I'm already A-U-G-H--

01:01:19.330 --> 01:01:23.000
So every Scottish MacLachlan
was an Irish McLoughlin?

01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:24.800
This is where it gets very complicated

01:01:24.800 --> 01:01:28.800
because if you, it's very
difficult to research this stuff

01:01:28.800 --> 01:01:32.270
and it's like, first of
all, within McLaughlin,

01:01:32.270 --> 01:01:35.310
spelled my way, you go back

01:01:35.310 --> 01:01:40.180
and there's two completely
distinct, unrelated groups

01:01:41.150 --> 01:01:43.793
and there's really no way to
know which one you're from.

01:01:44.690 --> 01:01:49.050
But one of those groups
went across the channel

01:01:50.320 --> 01:01:53.887
to Scotland and became
the MacLachlans but then,

01:01:53.887 --> 01:01:57.690
there was another tradition
that basically says that

01:01:59.130 --> 01:02:03.090
the McLaughlins spelled
my way can be traced back

01:02:03.090 --> 01:02:05.530
to MacLachlan but that's a little bit less

01:02:05.530 --> 01:02:07.850
of a popular tradition.

01:02:07.850 --> 01:02:09.800
This is very, the records were horrible.

01:02:09.800 --> 01:02:11.710
One of the reasons that there's
all the different spellings

01:02:11.710 --> 01:02:13.370
is that they couldn't spell.

01:02:13.370 --> 01:02:14.727
Somebody would just be
like, "What's your name?"

01:02:14.727 --> 01:02:17.098
"McLaughlin," and MacLachlan,
he would just write it down

01:02:17.098 --> 01:02:20.160
and so there's literally
like 200 different ways

01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:21.700
to spell it if you go into the book

01:02:21.700 --> 01:02:23.400
of Scottish names or whatever.

01:02:23.400 --> 01:02:26.500
And when we were at the
castle, there was a bridge

01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:29.271
that you could cross and on the bridge

01:02:29.271 --> 01:02:33.960
where people who had
donated money to this bridge

01:02:33.960 --> 01:02:36.820
and one of the people
was a McLaughlin spelled

01:02:36.820 --> 01:02:41.820
exactly my way that said,
McLaughlin with so-and-so clan,

01:02:43.670 --> 01:02:47.220
and they identify with this, so--

01:02:47.220 --> 01:02:48.250
He's hoping the same thing

01:02:48.250 --> 01:02:50.660
you were hoping at this point.

01:02:50.660 --> 01:02:52.010
What I'm saying is that--

01:02:53.886 --> 01:02:55.060
What you're saying is that

01:02:55.060 --> 01:02:56.910
your mom broke her ankle for nothing.

01:03:00.120 --> 01:03:01.784
Or something.
No now I gotta--

01:03:01.784 --> 01:03:02.790
Depending on--
Now I gotta take a trip

01:03:02.790 --> 01:03:04.560
to Ireland.
Yeah you do.

01:03:04.560 --> 01:03:06.000
Yeah you do!

01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:07.903
That's right, do they have castles?

01:03:07.903 --> 01:03:09.753
Yeah they got castles.
They got castles.

01:03:10.700 --> 01:03:12.250
So--
And sheep.

01:03:12.250 --> 01:03:14.303
That made it a little less special.

01:03:16.230 --> 01:03:17.560
Listen man, it's--

01:03:17.560 --> 01:03:19.333
But ultimately--
It's all what you

01:03:19.333 --> 01:03:20.958
wanna believe.
Well first of all,

01:03:20.958 --> 01:03:24.060
it ultimately is impossible to trace

01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:27.760
and you can't really know
but traditionally speaking,

01:03:27.760 --> 01:03:31.880
it is most likely that the McLaughlin name

01:03:31.880 --> 01:03:35.260
that I have came from someone in Ireland.

01:03:35.260 --> 01:03:37.860
I can't trace it because
we don't have good,

01:03:37.860 --> 01:03:39.360
my records aren't good enough.

01:03:41.170 --> 01:03:43.570
But maybe there's some Scotland connection

01:03:43.570 --> 01:03:46.240
but it's definitely not a
definitive, like I know,

01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:49.620
I can trace it, I should
definitely pay thousands

01:03:49.620 --> 01:03:51.160
of dollars to send my
whole family over there

01:03:51.160 --> 01:03:53.358
so we can put on kilts and
have my mom break her ankle.

01:03:53.358 --> 01:03:55.642
It's not that kinda connection.

01:03:55.642 --> 01:03:57.870
It's not that definitive.

01:03:57.870 --> 01:04:00.966
It's not ankle-breaking
in four places definitive.

01:04:00.966 --> 01:04:01.799
Oy.

01:04:04.074 --> 01:04:05.537
Wonder what'll happen in Ireland.

01:04:05.537 --> 01:04:06.760
Oh man.
Wonder what'll get broken

01:04:06.760 --> 01:04:07.593
in Ireland.

01:04:12.330 --> 01:04:14.308
Had a great time otherwise.
You had a great time.

01:04:14.308 --> 01:04:15.527
I mean it was a great vacation.

01:04:15.527 --> 01:04:16.500
You know what--
A lot of good stories.

01:04:16.500 --> 01:04:19.890
A lot of memories, lot of
memories, lot of good memories.

01:04:19.890 --> 01:04:22.600
One in particular but a lot of memories.

01:04:22.600 --> 01:04:23.720
Yeah.

01:04:23.720 --> 01:04:25.053
No one will be the same.

01:04:25.900 --> 01:04:28.517
And you could still be,
everyone can be better

01:04:28.517 --> 01:04:30.480
as a result of this, you know.

01:04:30.480 --> 01:04:35.100
With her recovery, she's
gonna be much more confident

01:04:35.100 --> 01:04:38.351
in physical therapy and
to go back to this trainer

01:04:38.351 --> 01:04:41.459
than if she would have
just broken her ankle--

01:04:41.459 --> 01:04:43.657
That's true.
Back and she hadn't had

01:04:43.657 --> 01:04:47.670
the trainer experience,
a lot of people just,

01:04:47.670 --> 01:04:49.340
they flake out on physical therapy

01:04:49.340 --> 01:04:51.200
and they don't believe in it but she,

01:04:51.200 --> 01:04:53.330
once you experience the
benefits of something like that,

01:04:53.330 --> 01:04:55.310
she's much more likely to say, hey,

01:04:55.310 --> 01:04:59.380
I want to recover everything
that I experienced

01:04:59.380 --> 01:05:01.620
in preparation for the trip and leading up

01:05:01.620 --> 01:05:05.730
to the one last step that
I would have just taken

01:05:05.730 --> 01:05:09.460
a little bit differently, this
never would have happened.

01:05:09.460 --> 01:05:10.700
I was trying to make you feel better

01:05:10.700 --> 01:05:11.930
but I keep going back to that.

01:05:11.930 --> 01:05:15.540
Yeah I think that the,
I completely agree that

01:05:16.730 --> 01:05:19.690
any sort of tragedy like
this is an opportunity

01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:23.210
without doubt, you know,
it's obviously affecting

01:05:24.723 --> 01:05:27.530
the relationship, the fact that my dad has

01:05:27.530 --> 01:05:31.420
to basically serve her when he's there

01:05:31.420 --> 01:05:34.500
is gonna do something
for their relationship.

01:05:34.500 --> 01:05:36.890
That's inevitable and the
way that her community's

01:05:36.890 --> 01:05:40.650
kinda coming around her and
showing her that they love her.

01:05:40.650 --> 01:05:43.600
There are definitely positives
that can be taken out of it.

01:05:46.020 --> 01:05:48.410
And I do hope, I mean my hope is that yes,

01:05:48.410 --> 01:05:50.090
she is going to make a full recovery

01:05:50.090 --> 01:05:53.453
and get back into her training.

01:05:54.920 --> 01:05:57.640
I just don't want her
to get too comfortable

01:05:58.660 --> 01:06:03.660
in basically, in a wheelchair,
you know what I'm saying?

01:06:04.550 --> 01:06:07.963
That's my fear is that
just be like, okay well,

01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:11.800
I can't really do things anymore.

01:06:11.800 --> 01:06:13.610
I'm not saying that that's
what her mentality is

01:06:13.610 --> 01:06:16.453
but I don't want that being a temptation.

01:06:17.900 --> 01:06:22.377
So anyway, that's my trip in a nutshell.

01:06:22.377 --> 01:06:23.313
Wow.

01:06:24.630 --> 01:06:27.187
I have some other things but
we're basically out of time

01:06:27.187 --> 01:06:29.250
and that's really all
that I needed to say.

01:06:29.250 --> 01:06:31.090
Thanks for taking us on that trip.

01:06:31.090 --> 01:06:33.240
Wow, I'm still kinda reeling

01:06:34.420 --> 01:06:36.990
from that left turn at the end.

01:06:36.990 --> 01:06:41.990
And I will say that my
wife is the perfect person

01:06:45.070 --> 01:06:46.880
for situations like this.

01:06:46.880 --> 01:06:51.880
Like she is so good at
talking someone through

01:06:54.900 --> 01:06:59.900
a difficult situation in
way I am not good at at all.

01:07:00.120 --> 01:07:04.657
She was so good at talking, saying,

01:07:04.657 --> 01:07:06.497
"It's just a couple more steps.

01:07:06.497 --> 01:07:10.190
"Just one step at a time,"
very simple, comforting things.

01:07:10.190 --> 01:07:12.360
After the injury.
And also,

01:07:12.360 --> 01:07:15.860
that night we got home after
she had her leg in a cast

01:07:15.860 --> 01:07:19.210
and the next day was the one
we had slated to go play golf

01:07:19.210 --> 01:07:23.507
in St. Andrews and my dad was
like, "Well I'm not gonna go.

01:07:23.507 --> 01:07:25.410
"I need to stay with your mom."

01:07:25.410 --> 01:07:26.470
She needed help doing everything.

01:07:26.470 --> 01:07:28.480
She needed help using the bathroom.

01:07:28.480 --> 01:07:30.963
She needed somebody with her at all times.

01:07:32.490 --> 01:07:35.477
And Jessie was like, "I
am not letting your dad

01:07:35.477 --> 01:07:37.637
"not go play golf, that
was one of the things

01:07:37.637 --> 01:07:39.157
"that you had your heart set on

01:07:39.157 --> 01:07:40.910
"and I know he's feeling that way,"

01:07:40.910 --> 01:07:44.120
so she stayed with her
the entire day that day.

01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:46.053
Didn't go into town or do anything.

01:07:47.160 --> 01:07:50.040
And stayed with her so shout-out to Jessie

01:07:50.040 --> 01:07:52.990
for being a voice of
reason in difficult times

01:07:52.990 --> 01:07:56.640
but also watching after my
mom so we could go play golf

01:07:56.640 --> 01:07:59.260
because even though I was
thinking the whole time,

01:07:59.260 --> 01:08:01.713
I feel kinda bad, my mom's back there

01:08:01.713 --> 01:08:05.917
with a broken leg, I had
a great time playing golf.

01:08:05.917 --> 01:08:10.020
I mean it was a
once-in-a-lifetime experience

01:08:10.020 --> 01:08:13.397
and one of the things I will
also post on my Twitter,

01:08:13.397 --> 01:08:17.690
@rhettmc, is I did a bunch, not a bunch,

01:08:17.690 --> 01:08:22.300
but a good number of 360 photos,

01:08:22.300 --> 01:08:24.050
kinda like what I did when
we did the one in here

01:08:24.050 --> 01:08:25.950
and show everybody what it looks like

01:08:25.950 --> 01:08:27.680
at the round table of dim lighting.

01:08:27.680 --> 01:08:29.290
I did that as we went around.

01:08:29.290 --> 01:08:31.430
It took me a little bit late
in the trip to start doing that

01:08:31.430 --> 01:08:34.380
but both in Scotland and
England when I was in places

01:08:34.380 --> 01:08:37.078
of note, I would get a
360 photo that you can go

01:08:37.078 --> 01:08:39.690
over to the site that I posted 'em,

01:08:39.690 --> 01:08:42.160
kinda enter into that world yourself.

01:08:42.160 --> 01:08:43.360
Oh that's cool.
Including when we were

01:08:43.360 --> 01:08:44.470
playing golf at St. Andrews.

01:08:44.470 --> 01:08:46.820
Just watch your step.

01:08:46.820 --> 01:08:47.653
Yeah.

